  "keyTakeaways": [
    "Canada, the largest buyer at $3.77B, has charged a 50% surtax on U.S. perfume (3303), lip, eye and nail make-up (3304.10–3304.30) and other hair preparations (3305.90) since September 8, 2026; CUSMA origin does not exempt them. Skin care, shampoo, toothpaste, deodorant and flavor bases stay duty-free.",
    "In China, U.S. perfume, make-up, shampoo, toothpaste and deodorant pay about 38% (3% normal rate + 25% 2019 counter-tariff + 10% extra) unless the importer holds an exclusion; U.S. sales there fell 24% in 2025.",
    "The EU cut its tariff on almost all U.S. Chapter 33 goods to zero from July 1, 2026, removing 6.5% on deodorants, shaving and bath products and up to 7% on citrus oils; only food and drink flavor bases (3302.10) keep EU duties.",
    "Two China dates matter: its exclusions from the 2019 counter-tariffs end on December 31, 2026, and its extra tariff could rise from 10% to 34% on January 10, 2027."
  ],
